# Hyper-Vibe Coding Course Live Truth Audit (GitHub · Supabase · Vercel · Stripe)

## Executive overview

The Hyper-Vibe Coding Course stack (GitHub repo, Supabase project `tlavrxiaegbtyfmjfdcz`, Vercel deployment, Stripe TEST-mode) is now in a materially safer state than before this session.
Two real learner-facing production blockers were fixed:

- M1 quiz no longer flashes a false "Quiz coming soon." empty state; it uses an explicit loading state and renders the live hv_quizzes payload consistently.
- Dashboard "My learning" no longer stays empty for learners with module completions; it now surfaces HV module progress when legacy enrollments are empty.

The browser Supabase client has migrated from legacy `anon` JWT-style keys to the new **publishable** key family (`sb_publishable_*`) with no requests to the deleted `yhtmui` project and no legacy-`anon` marker left in the built frontend bundle.[^1]

A hard gate around M11/M12 ensures their legacy vs AI Agents 2.0 curriculum decision is explicitly deferred and protected from accidental edits.

Supabase’s API key migration model is now aligned with the project’s real state: legacy `anon` and `service_role` keys coexist with new publishable and secret keys, and the system is part-way through a deliberate staged migration in line with Supabase’s deprecation timeline.[^2][^3]

The remaining serious risk is **unretired legacy server-side keys**, particularly the Stripe webhook and other Edge Functions, Discord bot code, agents, and scripts still referencing `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` or shared secret naming.

